# ============================================
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cert
*.secret

# ============================================
# VS Code Extension Packages
# ============================================
*.vsix

# ============================================
# Settings Exports with Credentials
# ============================================
*-settings-export*.json

# ============================================
# MCP Configuration (local/developer-specific)
# ============================================
.vscode/mcp.json
**/.vscode/mcp.json

# ============================================
# Security audit reports (may contain redacted findings)
# ============================================
.ptah/**
# ...except the task specs, which are tracked history: carriers, planning prose
# and review artifacts.
!.ptah/specs/
!.ptah/specs/**
# ...and the shared workspace analysis; its own .gitignore keeps machine-local files out.
!.ptah/analysis/
!.ptah/analysis/**
# Screenshots stay local: they are large binary evidence, not history.
.ptah/specs/**/*.png
.ptah/specs/**/*.jpg
.ptah/specs/**/*.jpeg
.ptah/specs/**/*.webp
.ptah/specs/**/*.gif
# ...except the GENERATED files inside them, which are re-excluded here.
# Later patterns win, so these come after the allow-list above.
#   .harvested.json  — written by skill-synthesis when it harvests a trajectory
#   README.md        — emitted by `renderSpecsReadme` on every index start
# Both are derived from the carriers beside them and rewrite themselves, so
# tracking them puts churn from an unrelated harvest or reindex into whatever
# commit happens to be open. registry.md is deliberately NOT here: it is also
# generated, but it is the human-readable index people link to.
.ptah/specs/**/.harvested.json
.ptah/specs/README.md
.agent-legacy/**
.github/agents/**
# ============================================
# Claude Code configuration (local except shared project configuration)
# ============================================
.claude/*

# Project-owned Claude assets are committed in full: agents, commands and
# output-styles here; skills further down, AFTER the broad `skills/` rule that
# would otherwise re-ignore the directory (the last matching rule wins).
# Everything else under `.claude/` (settings.local.json, worktrees, …) stays local.
# Known consequence (TASK_2026_361): harness-sync may report a committed skill
# copy as foreign/blocked on a machine whose manifest does not own it.
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/agents/**
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/**
!.claude/output-styles/
!.claude/output-styles/**

