!tools/mcp-bench/src/memory-skills/suites/skills/
!tools/mcp-bench/src/memory-skills/suites/skills/**
!tools/mcp-bench/fixtures/memory-skills/cassettes/skills/
!tools/mcp-bench/fixtures/memory-skills/cassettes/skills/**
# Project-owned `.claude/skills` — must sit AFTER the broad `skills/` rule above,
# because the last matching rule wins and `skills/` would re-ignore the directory.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/workflows/
!.claude/workflows/**
skills-lock.json
.remocn-fetch

apps/coverage/**
libs/frontend/webview-e2e-harness/test-results/**

# Developer scratch, matching the eslint `ignores` in eslint.config.mjs.
# Mutation-testing a fix copies a source file to `.bak`, stubs it out, runs the
# spec and restores it; scratch render/bundle harnesses land beside the code
# they drive. Ignoring them here makes "never a committed source file"
# structural rather than a convention someone has to remember — the eslint half
# alone once silently un-linted a tracked file that merely started with `tmp-`.
*.bak
tmp-scratch-*

# ptah:harness:begin
# Managed by Ptah. Derived copies of ~/.ptah/user — edit the source, not these.
# Delete this whole block to opt out, or set harness.manageGitignore to false.
.github/skills/
# ptah:harness:end
.ptah/specs/**/*.log

# tools/perf probe output (traces can be hundreds of MB)
tools/perf/out/
